    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 13th with a lineup heavily incentivized by dynamic platoon advantages and top-of-the-order positioning. **Junior Caminero** (67.36) headlines our projected production, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Jos\u00e9 Soriano and an optimal #3 slot. **Christian Yelich** (64.16) and **Dillon Dingler** (61.51) represent our next tier of elite starts; **Christian Yelich** is particularly intriguing as he leverages a massive 13% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against Aaron Nola, while **Dillon Dingler** continues to be a high-upside play due to his 14% platoon edge and the expectation of hitting cleanup. While **Trea Turner** (56.84) and **Yordan Alvarez** (60.26) face tougher hurdles against lefties, their pedigree and batting order status keep them firmly in the starting rotation.\n\nStrategic volatility defines the fringe of our lineup today, as we are waiting on official batting orders for several key bats. **Casey Schmitt** (48.43) remains a start despite facing a respectable arm in Ben Brown, as he gains value from an anticipated #3 spot and a favorable wind direction. On the bench, **Carson Benge** (52.34) was the most difficult exclusion; while his matchup against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez offers promise, his total efficiency score lagged behind our middle-infield starters, leading us to bench him to preserve game caps. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Caleb Durbin** (44.03), whose matchup against Jacob deGrom presents a significant SP skill penalty that nearly pushed him below our 40-point floor. Owners should track lineup confirmations for **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Trea Turner**, **Junior Caminero**, **Christian Yelich**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Kyle Schwarber**, as any shift out of the leadoff or cleanup spots will recalibrate their efficiency scores heading into first pitch.",
